\h Micah
\toc1 Micah
\toc2 Micah
\toc3 Micah
\mt1 Micah
\c 4
\v 6 On that day, says the Lord, I shall gather her who is broken, and I shall welcome her who is cast out, and those whom I drove away. 
\v 7 And I shall make her who was broken into a remnant, and her who was cast out into a mighty nation; and the Lord will reign over them on Mount Zion, from now and for evermore.
\c 5
\v 2 And you, Bethlehem, House of Ephratha, are you too few to be among the thousands of Judah? From you shall come forth for me One who is to be ruler in Israel; and his goings forth are from the beginning, from days of old.
\v 3 He will therefore give them up until the time when she, who is to give birth, gives birth; and then the remnant of their brothers and sisters will return to the children of Israel.
\v 4 And he will stand and see, and shepherd his flock in the power of the Lord; and they will live in the glory of the name of the Lord their God; for now he will magnified to the very ends of the earth.
